  "passage": {
    "text": "According to Hamel, bureaucracy is increasing because organisations are creating more rules and centralising decision-making. This has significant financial consequences. Research conducted by Hamel and his colleague Michele Zanini estimates that the effects of bureaucracy cost society approximately $3 trillion per year in the US alone. Structurally, organisations tend to resemble a pyramid, with the board of directors at the top and multiple layers of management below. At the bottom of this structure are the people who carry out the actual work.",
